Jesssica wrote:
> Is it better to delve as deep into the dungeon as possible, going
> downstairs whenever you find a staircase, or to explore every level
> before going down further?

You ask for opinions, not proven fact, I figure, so here goes.

Since monster difficulty partly by dungeon depth attained, yet does not
change at all depending on items found, in the general case it should
be better to explore as much as you can so long as you are not put in
danger by other means, like starving, by doing so.

One exception to this is when you have a specific strategy that being
of low level will help you, but I only know of the protection racket in
this regard.  Dive for victory can be useful for obtaining wishes
early, but first you have to get to it.  When I play I consider every
game precious, that is I try to win as many as I can, and neither of
these strategies is good for one's victory percentage.

